WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.780
We have 3.7 million farmers

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.290
and more than 10 million fish
farms all across Indonesia.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.300
The fish trading market
is a $10 billion market

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.530
already in Indonesia.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.470
The feed market is a $5 billion market

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.770
but that's only Indonesia.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.150
But if we see on the global scale,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.900
the aquaculture is a hundred
billion dollar market.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.543
My dream was to operate my own fish farms,

00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:29.730
1,000 of fish ponds.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.320
That was my dream.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.260
I met many farmers that operate 100 ponds,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.540
200 ponds, even 1,000 ponds.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.090
And when I spoke to many farmers,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.463
I saw similar problems
that the farmers face.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.420
All farmers know that the
feed cost is the biggest cost.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.700
It's 70% to 90% of the total cost

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.710
and currently done manually by labor.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.360
So the quality of the
feed that you produce

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.370
is really depending on whether the labor

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.050
feed your fish properly.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.400
And from that discussion,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.920
impulsively, it's just a spontaneous idea

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.247
that I pitch to the farmer,

00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:02.040
"Hey, what if I can build a machine

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.680
that you can feed your
fish from your phone?"

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.350
And if these problems is the
same with all of the farmers,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:09.931
then we even have much bigger opportunity.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.850
My name is Gibran Huzaifah.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.863
I'm CEO and co-founder of eFishery.

00:01:21.272 --> 00:01:25.320
As a child, I can say that
I grew up pretty poor.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.330
Both of my parents married quite early

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.980
so they didn't settle economically.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:35.640
But if I remember what it
feels like during my childhood,

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.280
it's all about, you know, happiness.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.160
So that part gave me an idea

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.920
that it's not always about
the wealth, the money,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.220
but it's about the
relationships that we build.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.070
When I started my own fish
farming back then in college,

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.620
there's not really an external problem

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.240
that I was trying to solve.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.550
It's just about solving my own problems

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.180
and tried to be independent
back then when I was in college.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.820
But it got me to a realization

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.150
that the massive opportunity
of the sector is really big,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.803
and that started eFishery from that point.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.150
Our approach is really how
we can help small scale

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:19.350
and small older farmers to
increase their productivity,

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.630
and provide efficiency
on their biggest cost,

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:22.463
which is feeding.

00:02:22.463 --> 00:02:25.560
So that's why we started on
building this eFishery feeder.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.230
So this is a machine to
feed the fish automatically

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.450
that is connected to the cloud
and connected to the sensor

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.040
that can sense the fish appetite.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.140
So it can improve the feed efficiency

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.850
or the feed conversion ratio,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:38.490
as well as on increasing
the growth of the fish

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.972
so they can shorten the harvest cycles.

00:02:40.972 --> 00:02:42.960
When they use this kind of technology

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.790
that these are radically affordable,

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.120
they only need to pay $10
per month to use this.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.290
They will see that their
farming practice has improved

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.581
because the technology is
embedded in their operations.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.980
This kind of process is
even more interesting

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.860
because this technology
opening new doors for us

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.570
to capture a lot of data information.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:05.130
How many feed that they're using?

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.080
What's the feed rate frequency per day?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.490
What brand of feed that they're using?

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.310
And the farmers can even
capture more data information

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.170
on how many fish that
they will be harvesting,

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.370
how many fish are there.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.210
We try to use the data
and build credit scoring

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.520
to connect farmers with
the financial institution

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.710
so they can receive the financing

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.540
from financial institutions directly.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.460
And we can also use the
data to connect farmers

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.410
to the downstream buyers.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.870
So all in all, it's all
about increasing the profit

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.663
of the farmers by leveraging
the data and technology.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.760
Each of the farmers has
received many benefit,

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.770
at least the productivity,

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:45.770
and their income is
increased from 40% to 200%.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.570
We saw many farmers
that started, you know,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.480
joining eFishery only on, like, two ponds

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.180
but right now, they own 20 ponds.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.260
So the productivity and their
income increased by 10 times,

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.207
only joining eFishery in one year.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.360
It was really challenging.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.640
It was not as easy as
I thought it would be

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.210
because when we had the product,
when I went to the farmers,

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.580
the farmers never really understood

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.050
why they need to use this product

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.330
because most of the farmers
are very traditional

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.980
and they've been doing it for decades.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.650
They've been feeding the fish for 20 years

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.960
and using traditional model.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.810
So they don't really know how this help

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.220
and whether this replace labor,

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.710
and labor is very cheap in Indonesia.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.380
But when I asked them why
they want to use eFishery,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.510
I thought it would be
about the technology,

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.150
and the solutions, the
benefit of the product itself,

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.263
but apparently not.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.860
What farmers appreciate
is about the community

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.220
that we need to build, about
the sense of belongings

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.623
on the bigger mission that we have.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.710
So I think that's the biggest lesson,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.660
that building a business is
not just about the numbers

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:55.050
and the metrics, but
really about the human side

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:58.260
and human relationship
that we need to maintain,

00:04:58.260 --> 00:04:59.463
to build, and to scale.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:07.130
So if I see eFishery contributing
to that larger ecosystem,

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.200
and see eFishery play a role on, you know,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.530
feed more people, but
also creating a livelihood

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.290
and also impacting that rural communities.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:18.600
So that's really what drives me,

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.730
what defines my definition of success.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:22.320
So it's not about, you know, the valuation

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:25.410
and my own wealth, but it's
really about how eFishery

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.660
can contribute to general, you know,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.110
success of those communities.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.300
We're currently doing a
pilot outside Indonesia.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.040
We did a pilot in Vietnam.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.350
We are currently doing a pilot in India.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.270
So we would like to prove the solutions

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.810
that coming from Indonesian innovators

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:46.830
building in Indonesia market
can actually take a big role

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.480
in the global aquaculture market.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.200
We're really excited about the future

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.970
because we're pioneering this sector.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.600
We're technically creating
this category of fish tech,

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.160
of aquaculture technology that
then has a really big upside

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.550
on building the market and
building the sector even further.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.140
And aquaculture is still currently

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.820
the fastest growing food
sector in the world.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.733
So for us, the sky is the limit.

